 "overview": "The CC Historical Commission and Historic District Commission evaluate historic significance, manage local historic districts, oversee demolition delay applications, and steward historic assets in Medford, Massachusetts. Meeting across 52 recorded sessions from April 10, 2023, through October 19, 2026, the body handles property preservation reviews, historical inventory surveys, and municipal preservation planning. Its work includes administering public hearings for demolition permits, managing Community Preservation Act projects at local historical sites, and integrating historic preservation provisions into updated municipal zoning policies. At its most recent meeting on October 19, 2026, the commission evaluated demolition applications, considered plans for veteran housing at 321 Winthrop Street, selected Lawrence Estates for its next state survey grant application, and reviewed updates on cemetery restoration and zoning incentives.",
