  {
   "name": "Demolition delay ordinance and property reviews",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Across its meetings, the commission regularly evaluates demolition applications for properties to determine historic significance and whether structures should be preferably preserved. When properties are designated as preferably preserved, the commission imposes demolition delays and collaborates with property owners to review revised architectural drawings or design modifications. The commission has also worked to refine its procedures, discussing bylaw enforceability, expedited review timelines, and exemptions for minor outbuildings. In late 2026, the commission continued to adjudicate demolition reviews and hold preferably preserved hearings for properties across the city.",
