  {
   "name": "Cross Street Cemetery archaeological and restoration work",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission pursued headstone conservation, records research, and site assessments at the historic Cross Street Burial Ground. Exploratory trenching at the former burial ground parcel revealed intact artifacts and human remains, prompting coordination with state agencies and multi-year site investigations. The commission allocated funds to repair relocated gravestones at Oak Grove Cemetery and restore veteran monuments. Work continued into 2026 with requests for Community Preservation Act funding, ground-penetrating radar bidding, and fence and stone restoration.",
