   "summary": "The commission engaged with city planning officials to review proposed developments, rezoning initiatives, and environmental reviews across Medford. Members examined municipal preservation models, such as Reading's preservation zoning ordinance, to explore incentives for owners preserving historic structures. The commission expressed interest in protecting pre-1900 structures during discussions surrounding the Salem Street corridor rezoning and broader zoning updates. As new zoning policies were approved for Medford Square and drafted for Boston Avenue, the commission focused on reconciling zoning incentives and design reviews with the city's demolition delay bylaws.",
